     5	The original P2 BLOCKING install-boundary defect is fixed. The late-hard-link checks and removal of arbitrary `verify()` are also sound. Adoption is still blocked by three HIGH gaps: ambiguous marker removal during archival, ambiguous pre-install ownership bookkeeping, and a `require_git(clean_paths=...)` check that does not actually prove a pathspec matched a tracked entry.
     6	
     7	## Ranked findings
     8	
     9	### HIGH — A post-effect active-marker unlink can leave installed destinations without an active mark
    10	
    11	The correct order is present: archive link, fsync `done/`, unlink active mark, fsync state directory at [records_txn.py:454–462](/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/records_txn/records_txn.py:454). However, `os.unlink(manifest)` is outside the restoration `try`.
    12	
    13	If an unlink wrapper performs the real unlink and then raises—or an asynchronous exception lands after the syscall took effect—the restoration block is never entered. The outer handler detects the missing mark and reports it at [records_txn.py:464–471](/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/records_txn/records_txn.py:464), but the next transaction is not blocked. All destinations are installed and the `done/` archive exists, so this is less severe than P2’s partial-install blocker, but a reported failure followed by a rerun can duplicate non-idempotent appends.
    14	
    15	The archive test makes unlink fail before calling the real operation at [test_records_txn.py:850–887](/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/records_txn/test_records_txn.py:850), so it cannot expose this window.
    16	
    17	Fix: put both unlink and the state-directory fsync inside the restoration scope; if either raises and the active path is absent, restore it from `done/`. Add real-unlink-then-raise tests for `OSError` and `AsyncInterrupt`, plus a mutant moving unlink outside the protected scope.
    18	
    19	### HIGH — Pre-install objects are registered after their mutating syscall
    20	
    21	Three bookkeeping assignments occur after the corresponding creation:
    22	
    23	- Manifest: `_excl(manifest)` then `marked = True` at [records_txn.py:423–425](/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/records_txn/records_txn.py:423).
    24	- Planned directory: `os.mkdir(p)` then `made.append(p)` at [records_txn.py:427–429](/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/records_txn/records_txn.py:427).
    25	- Temp: `_excl(temps[k])` then `staged.append(...)` at [records_txn.py:430–433](/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/records_txn/records_txn.py:430).
    26	
    27	For example, a temp open that creates the file and then raises leaves `staged` empty. With an existing destination directory, `_remove_all([], [])` succeeds and the active mark is removed at [records_txn.py:472–486](/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/records_txn/records_txn.py:472), leaving an orphan temp and reporting that every staged temp was removed. The analogous mkdir window leaves an unmarked directory. A post-effect manifest open can leave an unreadable active marker while raising ordinary `Refused`, not `RecoveryNeeded`.
    28	
    29	The real-subprocess staging kill is useful, but process death preserves the already durable mark; it does not test exception-driven cleanup through these registration gaps.
    30	
    31	Fix: track a conservative “ownership syscall in flight” state before each creation. If an exception occurs before ownership is unambiguously registered, retain the manifest and raise `RecoveryNeeded`; never delete a possibly foreign object. Add perform-then-raise and asynchronous cases for manifest open, temp open, and mkdir.
    32	
    33	### HIGH — `clean_paths` can still pass vacuously and its returned state is mutable
    34	
    35	At [records_txn.py:151–160](/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/records_txn/records_txn.py:151), existence plus empty porcelain output is treated as proof that a path is tracked. An existing empty directory matches no index entry and produces no status output, so it passes despite being untracked and vacuous. The current test covers a missing path, an untracked file, an ignored file, and literal glob characters, but not an existing no-match pathspec: [test_records_txn.py:1024–1039](/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/records_txn/test_records_txn.py:1024).
    36	
    37	Additionally, `seen["clean_paths"]` aliases `check["clean_paths"]`, and `require_git()` returns only a shallow dictionary copy at [records_txn.py:298–302](/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/records_txn/records_txn.py:298). Mutating the returned list changes both the internal check and its original baseline, allowing a path never checked at declaration time to pass the under-lock comparison.
    38	
    39	Fix: prove that each pathspec has an index match, for example with a read-only `git ls-files --error-unmatch` check and an updated command allowlist, or reject directories and paths outside the work tree with equivalent proof. Store immutable tuples internally and return/archive independent copies. Test an empty directory and mutation of the returned list.
    40	
