     7	## Ranked findings
     8	
     9	### HIGH — A failed existence probe is treated as proof that an in-flight creation had no effect
    10	
    11	At [records_txn.py:480](/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/records_txn/records_txn.py:480), cleanup is avoided only when:
    12	
    13	```python
    14	inflight is not None and os.path.lexists(inflight)
    15	```
    16	
    17	`os.path.lexists()` does not distinguish ENOENT from EACCES, EIO, or another `lstat()` error; it catches every `OSError` and returns `False`, as confirmed in the reviewed interpreter’s [posixpath.py:174](/home/yixunhu/miniconda3/envs/flac/lib/python3.10/posixpath.py:174).
    18	
    19	Consequently:
    20	
    21	1. A temp creation or `mkdir` takes effect and then raises.
    22	2. The subsequent `lstat` probe raises EIO/EACCES.
    23	3. `lexists()` reports `False`.
    24	4. The handler assumes “no effect,” removes the other registered debris, unlinks and fsyncs the active mark, and returns an ordinary pre-install `Refused`.
    25	5. The created temp or directory remains without an active recovery mark.
    26	
    27	That violates the claimed rule that absence is proven before cleanup and leaves an object created by the transaction undescribed by an active mark. The existing perform-then-raise tests at [test_records_txn.py:594](/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/records_txn/test_records_txn.py:594) only exercise a successful follow-up probe.
    28	
    29	Concrete fix: use `os.lstat()` directly and treat only `FileNotFoundError` as proven absence. Any other probe error must preserve everything and raise `RecoveryNeeded`. Audit the other control-flow uses of `lexists`, particularly marker restoration at lines 467 and 475–480, so an unknown result is never described as absence.
