    36	
    37	A kill, ENOSPC, I/O error, or concurrent edit can leave only the early files updated. In `docs_1105f`, it can also leave some destination copies present, causing a retry to refuse. The probability is low on a healthy local filesystem, but exposure is largest in `docs_1104g` and `docs_1105f`. No partial execution was observed: every target commit contains the intended complete set, and subsequent anchors progressed consistently.
    38	
    39	Concrete fix: precompute all outputs, stage them to same-directory exclusive temporary files, fsync them, record a transaction/recovery manifest, then rename only after every stage validates. On restart, refuse or recover an incomplete transaction. Recheck original-file hashes immediately before installation.
    40	
    41	### BLOCKING — The first three scripts write before all anchors are validated
    42	
    43	`docs_1104g` validates memory frontmatter and the MEMORY index only after many earlier writes; `docs_1104h` and `docs_1105a` similarly run `re.subn` validation after modifying repository records:
    44	
    45	- [`docs_1104g_decisions.py:207–226`](/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/docs_1104g_decisions.py:207)
    46	- [`docs_1104h_exp35_r0.py:117–138`](/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/docs_1104h_exp35_r0.py:117)
    47	- [`docs_1105a_decisions.py:90–93`](/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/docs_1105a_decisions.py:90)
    48	
    49	This contradicts their “every anchor checked before anything is written” contract.
    50	
    51	Concrete fix: read every destination and perform every count, regex, newline, nonexistence, and source check before the first write; build the final byte strings in memory.
    52	
    53	### HIGH — Safety checks disappear under `python -O`, and new files are not exclusively created
    54	
    55	The first three scripts use `assert` for date, anchor, and nonexistence checks. Optimization disables those checks. Examples are [`docs_1104g_decisions.py:14–25`](/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/docs_1104g_decisions.py:14), [`docs_1104h_exp35_r0.py:9–16`](/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/docs_1104h_exp35_r0.py:9), and [`docs_1105a_decisions.py:10`](/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/docs_1105a_decisions.py:10).
    56	
    57	New files use overwriting APIs after a separate existence check. `docs_1105f` also has a check/copy TOCTOU window: [`docs_1105f_handback.py:35–39`](/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/docs_1105f_handback.py:35), [`:70–74`](/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/docs_1105f_handback.py:70).
    58	
    59	Concrete fix: use explicit `if ...: raise SystemExit(...)` and `open(..., "xb")`/`O_CREAT|O_EXCL`; never use `assert` for operational safety.
