    82	### NIT — Time zone is asserted by prose, not by the clock
    83	
    84	The entry timestamps themselves came from `datetime.now().astimezone()` and none was in the future. However, the scripts append literal `EST` without checking the UTC offset; `docs_1105b`–`f` also lack a date guard. Example: [`docs_1105b_e2fail.py:14–17`](/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/docs_1105b_e2fail.py:14).
    85	
    86	Concrete fix: use `ZoneInfo("America/New_York")`, format `%Z`, and explicitly validate the intended date/offset. Historic event times should come from a hashed source record, not typed literals.
