   115	## P4 SOP
   116	
   117	- Every mapped commit, including `9318995b`, has the required `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>` trailer.
   118	- Origin reflogs show fast-forward pushes throughout the range. No lost concurrent edit is visible. The branch subsequently advanced from `71721177` to `71eb142d`; `71721177` remains its direct ancestor.
   119	- Reflogs and available scratch files do not prove that `git pull --rebase` ran before every commit. A no-op pull may leave no movement, so this is unauditable—not evidence that the command was skipped.
   120	- No account email or apparent secret was added to the records. The HTTP request ID is an unnecessary operational identifier but is not an account credential.
   121	- The scripts perform filesystem record changes only; no package, environment, GPU, or process mutation is present.
   122	
   123	## P5 reusable pattern
   124	
   125	The next Planner script should use one shared record-update helper:
   126	
   127	1. Capture an immutable, SHA-256-bound source manifest and derive every factual field from it.
   128	2. Read every destination once; perform explicit anchor/date/nonexistence checks without `assert`.
   129	3. Build every final file in memory.
   130	4. Acquire a single-writer lock, verify the original hashes and branch/origin state again, and stage all outputs with exclusive creation.
   131	5. Install through a recovery-marked transaction with fsync and rollback/recovery support.
   132	6. Record the exact pull/rebase, commit trailer, and push result in an auditable command log.
   133	
   134	## Read-only probes performed
   135	
   136	I used `sha256sum`, `cmp`, `readlink`, `rg`, `sed`, `nl`, standard-library Python comparisons, `git log/show/diff/status/reflog/merge-base/rev-parse`, and inspection of the run worktree at `1f31c7a7`. I did not run any reviewed script, pytest, GPU command, package/environment command, or process probe, and modified no file.
     1	**Reviewer:** OpenAI Codex (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh, codex exec, read-only sandbox) · **Date:** 2026-11-05 · **Round:** Planner records tooling P2 (records_txn helper + docs_1105g / docs_1105h)
     2	
     3	**Verdict:** REQUEST-CHANGES
     4	
     5	The helper resolves most P1 requirements and has credible TDD/mutation evidence, but one install-error path can modify a destination and then delete the recovery manifest. Late hard-link validation and recovery-marker durability also need correction. Future Planner scripts must not adopt this revision as-is.
