     7	## Q1 — FAIL
     8	
     9	Confirmed working:
    10	
    11	- Full-SHA source verification and optional required review content.
    12	- No production `assert`; optimization does not remove checks.
    13	- One in-memory edit chain per canonical destination.
    14	- Exclusive same-directory staging, file fsync/readback, recovery manifest, atomic `link`/`rename`, directory fsync, and new-files-first ordering.
    15	- Existing recovery manifests refuse both construction and locked commit.
    16	- Aware `America/New_York` timestamps and an explicit date-check API.
    17	- Symlink refusal and exclusive final creation of new destinations.
    18	
    19	The transaction guarantee fails at [records_txn.py:349–377](/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/records_txn/records_txn.py:349). `installed` is incremented only after `os.link`/`os.replace` returns. A wrapper can perform the real operation and then raise; an asynchronous exception can land in the same interval. For the first install, `installed` remains zero, so the exception handler removes the manifest and reports that every destination is unchanged even though one changed.
    20	
    21	A hard kill during staging can also leave an unmarked temp because staging begins at line 326 while the recovery manifest is not created until line 342.
