exp_35 Codex code C3d fixes (HIGH 1, HIGH 2): the held reservation authenticated as its exact record at every step that acts on it; a GPU-listed PID with an unreadable identity is never approved
HIGH 1: create_reservation returns the sha256 of the exact bytes it wrote; the state keeps it in the held
record ({uuid, epoch, path, sha256}). reservation_reasons authenticates that record (the bytes' sha256, then
field by field, the epoch). It is authenticated before every lane decision in ready(), before and after the
60-s hand-over gap, right before the hand-over commit (the old and the new record), right before every
removal, and as the LAST step before a spawn (after the in-flight save: a spoiled record spawns nothing, the
chunk returns to planned, the state stays loadable). Removals go through release_reservation: unlink only a
file that IS the held record, through the inode just authenticated; a mismatch latches and unlinks nothing
(the hand-over and the final release). The first-spawn baseline is now set after the reservation step, so a
refused first reservation leaves a loadable state.

HIGH 2: listed_identity() is tri-state for a PID listed on our lane -- ok / gone (its identity unreadable AND
the re-queried compute table no longer lists it) / unreadable (still listed, or the table cannot be re-read:
never approved). The running-cell watch latches on an unreadable listed PID (the cell finishes); ready()
latches before any spawn or hand-over when the approved trainer is listed but unreadable.

