exp_35 Codex code C3d fix (HIGH 3) and Planner P1: the B-F probe's finalization idempotent only on the identical record (a restart at chunk 5 completes it without finalizing anew); one supervisor at a time (an exclusive lock next to the state)
HIGH 3: finalize_bf_probe accepts an already-finalized JSON UNCHANGED (nothing written) only when its bytes are
the finalizer's own output, its sidecar seals it, and its launch record is exactly the one this call would
write -- backend, overlay + launcher sha256, campaign digest, log path and the CURRENT log sha256; any other
record is refused ("already finalized ..."). The exp_25 mode never calls it. The supervisor's chunk-5 gate
keeps the ledger it recorded before a restart: the re-run's JSON / sidecar / log sha256 must equal it, else
the latch. The supervisor tests' FakeGates now finalize through the REAL collector finalizer (the production
rule), over a fake probe report awaiting finalization and a probe log carrying the backend evidence; the
restart test dies after the persisted finalization + ledger and before chunk 5's final guard.

P1: Supervisor.run() takes fcntl.flock(LOCK_EX | LOCK_NB) on <state>.lock BEFORE load_state and holds it until
the run ends; held elsewhere -> "SUPERVISOR REFUSED: another supervisor holds <lock>", rc 3, the state
untouched. The dry run never creates the lock; an existing one is probed with LOCK_SH | LOCK_NB and reported,
informational only.

