orbitrir_yaw_evidence_worklog.md-111-- **His training at the capture** — step 27,930 (epoch 6) at 20:19; his unshared rate over the last 1,000 steps 4.260 s/step (worst 500-step window 4.268, worst 100-step 4.29). The guard stops further spawns on a completed 500-step window > 9.712, a mean since our first spawn > 8.521, or a 100-step window > 9.950. The predictor (`(40,000 − step) × 3.5 s > 2 × planning + 30 min`) allows shared spawns until ≈ 08:40 EST Nov 6 (K8) / ≈ 09:10 (K1) at his ≈ 4.3 s/step; then the supervisor waits for his s43 to end (≈ 10:30–11:30 EST) and hands the lane to GPU 0.
orbitrir_yaw_evidence_worklog.md-112-- **The four supervisor rules** (Coder log `2026-11-05T19:06:20-05:00`): an unreadable GPU-listed PID latches unless a re-queried table no longer lists it; the reservation held as `{uuid, epoch, path, sha256}` and authenticated before every lane decision, around the hand-over, before every removal and as the last pre-spawn step; the probe restart through an idempotent finalizer + the persisted ledger; one supervisor at a time (`flock` on `<state>.lock`).
orbitrir_yaw_evidence_worklog.md-113-- **Accepted residuals (disclosed; Codex INT I6 + C3e)** — shared-card memory is not isolation (a co-tenant allocation spike can OOM either job despite the 10 GiB margin); NAS / CIFS stalls slow an in-flight cell and are never answered by a kill (a latch only prevents the next spawn); the guard and identity checks are sampled every ≤ 5 min, so very short-lived interference can be missed; the predictor carries the approved faster-training / long-cell forecast risk; GPU 0 can acquire a foreign process after the two free checks (the watch latches, the running cell is not terminated); userspace windows between the last authentication and the spawn and between the inode check and the unlink (microseconds); a trainer caught mid-exit and still listed latches (fail-closed); the dry run's shared-lock probe can make a starting supervisor refuse; a crash between the hand-over commit and the GPU 1 release latches at restart; the runner's own collector calls no longer write bytecode (PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 in the launch environment).
orbitrir_yaw_evidence_worklog.md:114:- **Pre-registered for later** — E5 (§14 A2, descriptive, after phase (ii)) will live at `analysis/yaw_robustness/exp35_e5_offorbit_pairs.py` (outside the runner's RELEVANT set, like `plot_yaw_curves.py`); its sha256 is recorded when it is written and Codex-reviewed, before it runs. Phase (ii) re-pins the external CANON manifest / checkpoint (`52c64b52…`, manifest `1e481447…`) at its own launch. Phase (ii) runs only on free cards, at the same H35 and digest, after the figure-cell ETA goes to Yixun.
