- **Accepted residuals (disclosed; Codex INT I6 + C3e)** — shared-card memory is not isolation (a co-tenant allocation spike can OOM either job despite the 10 GiB margin); NAS / CIFS stalls slow an in-flight cell and are never answered by a kill (a latch only prevents the next spawn); the guard and identity checks are sampled every ≤ 5 min, so very short-lived interference can be missed; the predictor carries the approved faster-training / long-cell forecast risk; GPU 0 can acquire a foreign process after the two free checks (the watch latches, the running cell is not terminated); userspace windows between the last authentication and the spawn and between the inode check and the unlink (microseconds); a trainer caught mid-exit and still listed latches (fail-closed); the dry run's shared-lock probe can make a starting supervisor refuse; a crash between the hand-over commit and the GPU 1 release latches at restart; the runner's own collector calls no longer write bytecode (PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 in the launch environment).
- **Pre-registered for later** — E5 (§14 A2, descriptive, after phase (ii)) will live at `analysis/yaw_robustness/exp35_e5_offorbit_pairs.py` (outside the runner's RELEVANT set, like `plot_yaw_curves.py`); its sha256 is recorded when it is written and Codex-reviewed, before it runs. Phase (ii) re-pins the external CANON manifest / checkpoint (`52c64b52…`, manifest `1e481447…`) at its own launch. Phase (ii) runs only on free cards, at the same H35 and digest, after the figure-cell ETA goes to Yixun.
- **ETA** — phase (i) ≈ 16.5 h of cells from 20:20 EST; shared on GPU 1 until ≈ 09:10 EST Nov 6, a wait until his s43 ends, then unshared on GPU 0: **phase (i) done ≈ Nov 6 12:30–15:00 EST** (re-estimated after chunks 3–4). Hard stops (no further spawn; report to Yixun): E1 mismatch, a guard violation, any receipt / verification failure, a failed overlay pre-flight, an invalid probe.
- **Monitoring** — a read-only Planner watcher (`scratchpad/r3a/exp35_phase_i_watch.sh`; exits on the supervisor's exit, a STOP LATCH or a gates_verified milestone; never signals anything) re-armed at each milestone (2 = E1, 4 = E2, 5 = the probe, then every ≤ 2 h).

